=== Core-v1 spec invariants ===
PASS   1  one-server Core-v1 scope and exact ordered 31-Tool catalog
          - one cdn-node server; exact ordered 31 Tools; ACME/zone-setting/privacy/Surge/rotation deferred
PASS   2  all 93 public schemas are closed, executable and tool-bound
          - 31 input + 31 data + 31 output-envelope schemas = 93 instance-tested groups
PASS   3  only main and BBR phase columns exist and every resting state has a writer/exit
          - main=19 states; BBR=11; every nonterminal state has an executable writer and exit
PASS   4  every Tool has closed policy metadata and a live declared error vocabulary
          - 33 error codes; zero unknown or dead; 31 closed policy objects
PASS   5  helper and broker operations are closed, caller-bound and never return plaintext
          - 25 helper and 22 broker operations, exact and caller-bound
PASS   6  xui_install is clean-host-only, fixed-adapter, secretless and owned-invertible
          - clean host only; pinned adapter; no caller command/path/URL or plaintext secret; owned inverse required
PASS   7  Cloudflare, certificate, Nginx and client profile bind one exact node hostname
          - one onboarding hostname authority; CF name = cert SAN = Nginx server_name = profile address/SNI/Host
PASS   8  BBR is limited to existing-kernel support and one owned drop-in
          - no kernel install/upgrade, bootloader/shared sysctl edit or reboot; two keys in one owned drop-in
PASS   9  mutations obey no-clobber and rollback only the same-run owned graph
          - 9 mutating Tools checked for owned receipts, before/after digests and rollback metadata
PASS  10  E2E acceptance requires authenticated traffic, expected egress, logs and prior-line health
          - latency/TLS/certificate/HTTP 101/static profile alone are structurally insufficient
PASS  11  Core Hooks are a closed deny/report layer with no deferred authority
          - six command-Hook events; deny/report only; Future-v2 names have no active Tool/state/authority
PASS  12  reporting lifecycle is derived from the open register and never self-claims READY
          - open register derived B=0/M=0/m=0; seven documents project STAGED_FINAL
PASS  13  every required ref has a declared producer and credential bytes stay outside MCP
          - 24 exact ref graph rows; 10 role/provenance flows; zero plaintext MCP credential paths
PASS  14  catalog markers, exact package bytes and closed private-key/runtime scanners match Core-v1
          - 1 exact Tool marker(s), 1 error marker(s); 9 exact frozen package files scanned as fatal UTF-8 raw-byte-bound text; STAGED_FINAL header, invariant body and all 8 raw covered-byte digests exact; no recognized structured private-key container or durable runtime value; opaque base64 remains a semantic-audit boundary
PASS  15  clean-host install uses a separate lease and must re-inventory/replan before dependents
          - NODE_INSTALL_P3 cursor completion gates fresh inventories, recompile and a non-inherited NODE_P2 approval
PASS  16  resolver-derived install/NODE plans, cursor and finite-inventory refresh are closed
          - resolver-derived install/NODE/BBR/rollback templates; cursor exact; active PT15M/PT10M refresh preserves only no-drift plans
PASS  17  rollback coverage, executor exclusivity and credential ownership are closed
          - 8 main external mutators derive eight reverse-order nodes; 11 fixed reconciliation observers; prefix replay forbidden
PASS  18  XUI broker composites and issuer-specific origin trust are exact
          - existing and same-run XUI credentials use fixed composites; public and Origin-CA trust paths remain distinct and verified
PASS  19  success predicates and BBR/main ordering cannot certify stale or false evidence
          - all success booleans are const true; BBR resolves before main seal and invalidates every post-change E2E predicate

